<name><surname>Lopez de Heredia</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name><name><surname>Lowe</surname><given-names>AJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Tutkova</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Munro</surname><given-names>RC</given-names></name><name><surname>Steinhoff</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Badeau</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Leaf morphological differentiation between Quercus robur and Quercus petraea is stable across western European mixed oak stands</article-title><source>Annals of Forest Science</source><year>2002</year></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Aas</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Taxonomical impact of morphological variation in Quercus robur and Q. petraea: a contribution to the hybrid controversy</article-title><source>Annales des Sciences Foresti&#x000e8;res</source><year>1993</year><volume>50</volume><fpage>107</fpage><lpage>113</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1051/forest:19930709</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dupouey</surname><given-names>JL</given-names></name><name><surname>Badeau</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Morphological variability of oaks (Quercus robur L., Quercus petraea (Matt.) Liebl., Quercus pubescens Willd.) in northeastern France: preliminary results</article-title><source>Annales des Sciences Foresti&#x000e8;res</source><year>1993</year><volume>50</volume><fpage>35</fpage><lpage>40</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1051/forest:19930702</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Howard</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Preszler</surname><given-na